          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Araunah said to David, “Let my lord the king take and offer up what seems good to him; here are the oxen for the burnt offering, and the threshing sledges and the yokes of the oxen for the wood. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.24.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.24.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 24:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "All this, O king, Araunah gives to the king.” And Araunah said to the king, “The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.24.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.24.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God accept you.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.24.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.24.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 24:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But the king said to Araunah, “No, but I will buy it of you for a price; I will not offer burnt offerings to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.24.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.24.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " my God which cost me nothing.” So David bought the threshing floor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.24.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.24.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
